senses.gloss:
(III)--(Maharloka) the fourth of the seven worlds;
1: Br. II. १९. १५५; M. ६०. 2; ६१. 1; १८४. २३; वा. १०१. १७.
Manus went to it after तपस् at Meru; Manus retire to this place when the periods of their duties are over; Gods like Ajitas, याम gan2as and आयुष्मन्तस् besides शुक्र, चाक्- षुष and others live in Maharloka;
2: Br. II. २१. २२; ३५. १७९, १९७; IV. 1. २५, ३३, १२२. वा. १०१. ४१, ५२, २०८; १०९. ४८.
the space between Dhruva and Jana; the residents of this loka possess mental powers to create any desired thing; even gods sacrifice to each other;
3: Br. IV. 2. 2, २१, ४०, ४२-3; वा. १०१. ४४.
created from व्याहृति.
4: Br. IV. 2. 2, २१; वा. १०१. २३.

--the neck of the पुरुष;
1: भा. II. 1. २८.
due to fire of San- कर्षण sages leave this to Janaloka;
2: Ib. VIII. २०. ३४.
the goal of yogins
3: Ib. XI. २४. १४.
(see Mahat) above the Pole Star; the residence of Kalpa people; at a distance of two crores of yojanas is Janaloka; becomes devoid of all beings at the end of the kalpa but not extinguished;
4: Vi. II. 7. १३.
burnt in the Pralaya.
5: Ib. VI. 3. २८-9.

--mind-born sons of ब्रह्मा, seven in num- ber, like भृगु, मरीचि, and Angiras;
1: Br. II. ३२. ८९, ९७; M. १४५. ८५; २४७. १०.
ety. from root ऋषि गतौ--meaning knowledge; great ज्ञानिन्स्;
2: Br. II. 6. ७१; वा. 7. ७४; ५९. ८२ and ८९.
their role in creation.
3: Ib. 7. ७५-6.

--the ankle of the creator;
1: भा. II. 1. २६; 5. ४१.
an underworld, where a गण of नागस् by name क्रोधवश live;
2: Ib. V. २४. 7, २९.
of gravel colour where are the cities of Virocana, the Asura chief and eight others.
3: वा. ५०. १२, ३४-7.

--an attribute of शिव;
1: Br. II. २६. 1; M. ४७. ७५; Vi. I. 8. 6.
presiding deity of the moon;
2: M. २४६. ६१; २६५. ४२.
in one of his previous births was कृष्ण;
3: Ib. ४७. 1.
of the Kai- लास hill;
4: Ib. ५४. 2.
drinks soma;
5: Br. IV. २८. ८९.
worshipped by लवण Asura;
6: Ib. III. 3. ७०; 7. ९१-2.
wor- shipped by the followers of भण्ड;
7: Ib. III. १०. १७; २१. ७६; २५. १४; ६०. २८; ७२. 3, १०८, ११६. IV. १०. २९; ११. ३२; १२. १६.
claimed भृगु as his son;
8: Ib. III. 1. ३८.
made the mind-born creatures of दक्ष not to grow; blessed सुरभी with eleven sons, Rudras;
9: Ib. III. 2. 4.
शुक्र went to, [page२-652+ ३४] for learning नीती;
१०: M. ४७. ७५.
roamed about in the महाकालवन with पार्वती;
११: Ib. १७९. 3.
in his name गार्ग्य performed penance for a son.
१२: Vi. V. २३. 3.
अवतार्स् of, were in Kali and not in the previous yugas;
१३: वा. २६. 2.
his मानसीतनु, Candra;
१४: Ib. २७. १६.
wife रोहिणी and son Budha.
१५: Ib. २७. ४७, ५६.

(I)--a काद्रवेय Na1ga;
1: Br. III. 7. ३३; M. 6. ४०; वा. ६९. ७०. Vi. I. २१. २१.
with the Hemanta sun;
2: Br. II. २३. १७; M. १२६. १८; वा. ५२. १७; Vi. II. १०. १३.
in the वैडूर्यशाला;
3: Br. IV. २०. ५४; ३३. ३६.
shaken by हिरण्य- कशिपु.
4: M. १६३. ५६.

--of Bali at the hands of भृगु;
1: भा. VIII. १५. 4;
its विधि observed by अम्बरीष.
2: Ib. IX. 4. ३१.

--Kamsa addressed the हस्तिप thus;
1: भा. X. ३६. २४ [1-4] and २५;
there was more than one महामात्र in charge of the elephant, कुवलयापीड; all of them were killed by कृष्ण.
2: Ib. X. ४३. १२ and १४; Br. III. ३८. २४.

--कामाक्षी;
1: Br. IV. १९. 8.
mother of ब्रह्मा, विष्णु and ईश;
2: Ib. IV. ३६. ५८; ३९. २१, १११; ४०. 5; वा. १०९. २३.
is त्रीपुराम्बिका;
3: Br. IV. ४१. 3; ४४. १११; ४३. ८५.
the goddess enshrined at Kara- वीर.
4: M. १३. ४१.

(V)--an Asura residing in रसातलम्;
1: Br. II. २०. ३९.
was pre- sent at तारक's coronation; a commander of तारक's force and had a chariot drawn by camels;
2: M. १४७. २८; १४८. ४२, ५०.
threw सावित्रम् अस्त्रम् against Kubera; defeated both नृऋति and वरुण and releas- ed Kujambha from the noose; सोमास्त्रम् and वायव्यास्त्रम् throwing out snow and wind, were sent to disable the Asuras, [page२-669+ ३३] when कालनेमि created a glowing fire by माया and removed the snow and wind etc;
3: Ib. १५०. ११३, १३५; १५१. १३.
found Mathana vanquished by जनार्दन and sent his शूल against जनार्दन and शक्ति against गरुड when जनार्दन repelled him and said: “You are to be killed by a woman; get away;
4: Ib. १५२. १७-24.
killed by दुर्गा.
5: Br. IV. २९. ७५ and ८८.

(I)--a Vindhyan tribe: पुष्पमित्र was a king;
1: Br. III. ७४. १८७.
born of Hamsa कालि;
2: Ib. III. 3. ७५.
the kingdom of.
3: वा. ९९. ३८६.

--the capital of the Haihayas, on the रेवा (नर्मदा). Entered by परशुराम who put to sword all the क्षत्रियस् to avenge his father's death; visited by Bala- राम;
1: भा. IX. १५. २२; १६. १७; X. ७९. २१.
originally a नाग capital with कर्कोटक sabha1;
2: Br. III. ३८. 2; ४६. ११; ६९. २६.
the place where कार्तवीर्य defeated कर्कोटक's son;
3: M. ४३. २९.
the place where रावण was imprisoned by कार्तवीर्यार्जुन;
4: Ib. ४३. ३८.
found- ed by माहिष्मान् and capital of कार्तवीर्यार्जुन.
5: Vi. IV. ११. 9, १९.

(II)--माधवी, (वसुन्धरा);
1: Vi. I. 4. 7, २५-28.
rescued by the Lord in वाराह disguise from पाताल; earth addressed the Lord in words of praise of his greatness;
2: Ib. I. 4. १२-24.
addressed by Sananda and other sages; the earth was rescued with mountains; and was divided into seven islands and created the four; भू and other worlds;
3: Ib. I. 4. २७-44.
see भूमी.
4: Ib. V. 1. ५७.

(II)--a Mt. a Kulaparvata of the भारत- वर्ष;
1: भा. V. १९. १६; VII. १४. ३२; Br. II. १६. १८; M. ११४. १७, ३१; १२४. २१; वा. ४५. ८९; Vi. II. 3. 3.
sacred to Indra and Hari and fit for श्राद्ध;
2: Br. III. १३. १७.
परशु- राम's penance here for १२ years, twice;
3: Ib. III. ४४. ३६; ४६. २९; भा. X. ७९. १२; IX. १६. २६.
अश्वमेध at;
4: Br. III. ४७. ३९, ४५; ५६. २३; ५७. 1; ५८. 3; IV. २१. 2; ३१. १७; ४४. ९९.
during the war with भण्ड, the देवी enclosed M. all round by a wall of fire;
5: Ib. IV. २६. १७-32.
rivers taking their origin from.
6: वा. ४५. १०६.

(I)--(शिव): cursed the seven sages to be born in every epoch;
1: Br. II. २७. ४७; III. 1. 9.
got वृष (bull) from सुरभी for his standard;
2: Ib. III. 3. ७८-79.
lived long in his father-in-law's house after marriage; Meru insulted him as poor and useless when उमा insisted on her husband to go to his house; he went to Benares after which it became Avimukta;
3: Ib. III. ३१. ३५. ६७. ३२, ६०.
also ब्रह्मा;
4: Ib. IV. 1. २०३; 2. २२१, २५७; 4. ३५, ७३; 7. ४९; १४. १८.
Stambha; कापालि on earth for having removed one face of ब्रह्मा; to get rid of this brahmicide शिव's service to कामाक्षी at काञ्ची; blessed for his समाधि; bathed in पञ्- casaras and found himself at काशि, from there to काञ्ची; Jyo- तिर्मयिभिक्ष given; the कपाल dropped out and he was relieved;
5: Ib. IV. ४०. ५२-59.
blessed Kubera to be the lord of the यक्षस् for his penance at the confluence of the नर्मदा and the कावेरी.
6: M. १८१. 3-5; १८५. १२; १८९. १०.
Praise of, by काव्य.
7: वा. ९७, १६२-202.

(II)--as cosmos; hence अचिन्त्यात्म but the source of all beings; Brahmanas from face, क्षत्रियस्, from breast, वैश्यस् from the thighs and शूद्रस् from the feet;
1: वा. 9. १२२.
created the world, men, devas, asuras, constellation, night, day, Vedas, etc.;
2: Br. I. 5. ९५.
the smallest atom among the प्रकृतिस्, never failing, absolute; formless, and of form; the darkness becomes illumination by the contact of तेजस्;
3: वा. १०१. २२६.
the six angas of; all wise, all satiating, ever arousing, all free, eternally powerful, and of undiminished strength;
4: Ib. १२. ३१-3.
a महायोगि;
5: Ib. २१. ३६.
लोकेश, worshipped in different ways.
6: Ib. ४९. १७१.

--the Goddess enshrined at महाकाल;
1: M. १३. ४१.
a name of ललिता;
2: Br. IV. १०. 7; १४. 3; २८. ८९; २९. १०२; ४०. 2.
गा and विरूपा dropped out of the face of [page२-673+ २८] महेश्वर; also रुद्राणी and महादेवी; was Mati, स्मृति, and Buddhi; asked by महादेव to bring the world under control by Yoga.
3: वा. २३. 5.
